You know, I actually really like that idea. I would want to do some
graphical editing for it, though, so that in both panels the "[to'e]
rodsi'u" are in the same order.

So, how about, respectively:

{lo mi xance cu sepsi'u .i lo mi xance cu *to'e* sepsi'u} (Picture edited
to reverse hands apart/together order.)
{ko'a kansi'u xabju .i ko'e *tol*kansi'u xabju)

Which has the additional benefit of showing that the valsi "to'e" and the
rafsi "tol" are equivalent?

